* 12AX7 triode, model by Norman Koren (1996), rewritten for ngspice B sources.
* Pins: plate (P), grid (G), cathode (K)
.subckt 12AX7 P G K
.param MU=100 EX=1.4 KG1=1060 KP=600 KVB=300 RGI=2000
.param CCG=2.3p CGP=2.4p CCP=0.9p
* Auxiliary voltage E1 (Koren): V(P,K)/KP * ln(1 + exp(KP*(1/MU + V(G,K)/sqrt(KVB + V(P,K)^2))))
BE1 e1 0 V={ V(P,K)/KP * ln(1 + exp(min(KP*(1/MU + V(G,K)/sqrt(KVB + V(P,K)*V(P,K))), 80))) }
RE1 e1 0 1G
* Plate current: 2*E1^EX/KG1 for E1>0, otherwise 0
BG1 P K I={ 2*pow(max(V(e1),0), EX)/KG1 }
RCP P K 1G
C1 G K {CCG}
C2 G P {CGP}
C3 P K {CCP}
* Grid current when the grid is positive
R1 G g5 {RGI}
D3 g5 K DX
.model DX D(IS=1n RS=1 CJO=10p TT=1n)
.ends 12AX7
